## Functions on the iterator trait

Of course, a `for` loop isn't the only way to consume an iterator. There are several functions on the iterator trait that consume the iterator as well. Many of these have useful secondary purposes. For instance, the `sum()` function on the iterator trait will consume an iterator of integer or floating-point values and return the sum of the values. Similarly, the `max()` and `min()` functions will return the highest or lowest element after consuming the iterator. These functions depend on the items we're iterating over being additive or comparable and are conditioned on the proper traits.

